cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RAGStrike: An Extensible Offensive Security Evaluation Framework for RAG Systems"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-31
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/ragstrike"
abstract: >-
  RAGStrike is an extensible offensive security evaluation framework for
  retrieval-augmented generation systems. Attack packs are discovered from a
  manifest rather than registered in code; detection is deterministic and
  canary-based rather than model-judged; risk scores are arithmetic a reader can
  reproduce by hand; and remediation text is retrieved from a reviewed catalog
  rather than generated. It ships with a differential lab -- VulnerableRAG and
  SecureRAG -- so that the scanner's own true-positive and false-positive
  behaviour can be measured rather than assumed.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - large language models
  - prompt injection
  - security testing
  - OWASP LLM Top 10
authors:
  - family-names: Patil
    given-names: Digvijay
